WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.736
-President Trump met Russian
President Vladimir Putin

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:05.504
in Finland today, and delivered

00:00:05.504 --> 00:00:08.408
one of the most surreal
performances by a president

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:09.775
in modern American history.

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:12.045
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:16.549
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.617
Even before he got to Finland,

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:20.419
Trump's foreign trip
was one of

00:00:20.419 --> 00:00:22.722
the more disastrous ones
in recent memory.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:25.124
He was in the U.K.,
where he met Queen Elizabeth,

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:26.893
and he immediately
embarrassed himself

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.595
by breaking royal protocol,

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:31.297
and wandering aimlessly
in front of her.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:35.869
♪♪

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:43.643
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:47.279
The Queen
just disappeared behind Trump.

00:00:47.279 --> 00:00:49.582
It's like a royal eclipse.

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:50.916
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:54.119
The only thing missing was Trump
staring directly at it.

00:00:54.119 --> 00:00:55.721
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:57.690
Although, seriously,
you're telling me

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.293
this guy only weighs 239 pounds?

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:01.461
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:04.597
He's so wide,
he completely covered a monarch.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:05.898
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:08.768
He's David Copperfielded
the Queen.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:10.403
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.871
Trump was also asked during his
trip about negotiations

00:01:12.871 --> 00:01:15.608
between Britain and the
European Union over Brexit.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.844
In particular,
he was asked about the prospect

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:20.680
of a hard Brexit,
which would involve the U.K.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.216
completely leaving
the E.U. single market,

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:24.684
and it was clear from his answer

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:28.254
that Trump had absolutely no
idea what he was talking about.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:30.423
In fact, it almost seemed
like he had never even

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.925
heard the term
hard Brexit before.

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:34.427
-Because you are
going to the U.K.,

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:37.630
what will be your message
on Brexit?

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.665
-Well, Brexit is...

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:41.467
You know, I've been
reading a lot about Brexit

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:42.735
over the last couple of days,

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.737
and it seems to be turning
a little bit differently,

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:47.340
where they're getting
at least partially involved

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.243
back with the European Union.

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:53.413 line:0%
-Is it heartbreaking?

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:54.814 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.782
-Oh, hard Brexit, I see.

00:01:56.782 --> 00:01:59.252
I thought you said
it was heartbreaking.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:02.188
I said that might be going
a little bit too far.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:03.756
Heartbreak?

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:04.790
Is it heartbreaking?

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.458
A lot of things
are heartbreaking.

00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:09.695
No, I would say that, you know,
Brexit is Brexit.

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:12.298
-Oh!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:15.934
Well, he's not wrong.
Brexit is Brexit.

00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:18.470
Although I beg reporters
at his next press conference --

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:21.774
someone ask him where
the word "Brexit" comes from.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.042
I bet he has no idea.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:24.810
"Brexit, I think everyone knows,

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:28.381
is the most
important meal of the day."

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.650
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.851
"You gotta have your Brexit.

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:33.653
Some mornings,
I have two Brexits."

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.488
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.657
If Trump weren't
so irredeemably awful,

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:40.526
his stupidity would almost be...
-Heartbreaking.

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:43.262
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:46.398
It would be hard Brexit.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:46.398 --> 00:02:48.835
But Trump --
Trump's answer managed

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:50.402
to make even less sense
after that.

00:02:50.402 --> 00:02:54.140
Watch as he somehow manages to
ramble from the topic of Brexit

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.576
to protesters
to how many electoral votes

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.510
he won in the 2016 election,

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.746
while also making clear
that he doesn't even know

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:03.283
which countries
are a part of the U.K.

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:05.151
-I just want
the people to be happy.

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:07.353
They're great people,
and I do think I have --

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:08.454
Sure, there'll be protests,

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:09.621
'cause there
are always protests,

00:03:09.621 --> 00:03:11.491
but I think there were --

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:13.893
There were protests the night
of the election, both ways.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.362
So, you know,
we had a great night.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:19.131
Uh, protests.
There might be protests.

00:03:19.131 --> 00:03:23.002
But I believe
that the people in the U.K. --

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.403
Scotland, Ireland --

00:03:24.403 --> 00:03:27.005
As you know,
I have property in Ireland.

00:03:27.005 --> 00:03:28.574
I have property all over.

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:32.211
I think that those people --
they like me a lot.

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:34.480
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.983
-Oh, my God.
Ireland is not part of the U.K.

00:03:37.983 --> 00:03:42.121
They famously fought,
like, a ton of wars over it.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.523
Seriously, if you
don't believe me, Donald,

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:45.924
I dare you to go
into any pub in Ireland

00:03:45.924 --> 00:03:47.860
and tell them that
they are part of the U.K.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.028
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:51.664
Then -- Then you can use
their free healthcare

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:54.267
to get the pint glass
removed from your rectum.

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:56.335
But if you thought --

00:03:56.335 --> 00:04:00.039
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:02.508
If you thought
all of that was bad,

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:04.610
it was nothing
compared to Trump's performance

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:05.578
today with Putin.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:07.246
Before and during the summit,

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:10.082
Trump was obviously very eager
to impress Putin.

00:04:10.082 --> 00:04:12.051
At a press conference
in Brussels last week,

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:14.353
for example, Trump said,
"Hopefully someday,

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:16.255
maybe he'll be a friend."

00:04:16.255 --> 00:04:18.390
Now compare that
to what Trump had to say

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:19.993
about our
European allies yesterday

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:21.560
during an interview in Scotland.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.295
Trump was asked
who his biggest foe is.

00:04:23.295 --> 00:04:25.030
Now, you might expect
that the country

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.032
that invades its neighbors,
interferes in our elections,

00:04:27.032 --> 00:04:29.168
and uses nerve gas
on foreign soil

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:30.702
might be the first
to come to his mind,

00:04:30.702 --> 00:04:33.138
but, of course,
Trump had a different answer.

00:04:33.138 --> 00:04:34.573
-Who's your biggest competitor,

00:04:34.573 --> 00:04:36.943
your biggest foe,
globally, right now?

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:39.278
-Well, I think we have
a lot of foes.

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:41.314
I think the European Union
is a foe,

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:43.215
what they do to us in trade.

00:04:43.215 --> 00:04:45.284
Now, you wouldn't think
of the European Union,

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:46.786
but they're a foe.

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:49.989
Russia's a foe,
in certain respects.

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:54.226
China is a foe economically,
certainly, they're a foe,

00:04:54.226 --> 00:04:56.295
but that doesn't mean
they're bad.

00:04:56.295 --> 00:04:58.531
-No, that's exactly
what that means.

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:00.099
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:03.235
If you call someone a foe, that
means you think they're bad.

00:05:03.235 --> 00:05:06.706
You never heard Batman say
"The joker is my greatest foe,

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.474
but other than that,
he's a really good dude."

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:09.474
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.474 --> 00:05:11.677
Also, the real foe
is whoever said,

00:05:11.677 --> 00:05:13.713
"This is the best hat
for your interview."

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:15.214
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:16.449
"Are you sure?

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:18.751
Are you sure
it's not too giant and white?"

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:20.219
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:23.322
And once Trump got to Finland,
the charm offensive continued.

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:25.457
Trump made clear
that he was desperate

00:05:25.457 --> 00:05:28.260
to get in Putin's good graces
by repeatedly offering

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.296
nothing but gushing praise

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:32.765
for Russia's hosting
of the World Cup.

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:35.100
-I also want
to congratulate Russia

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:39.037
and President Putin for having
done such an excellent job

00:05:39.037 --> 00:05:41.574
in hosting the World Cup.

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:44.176
It was really
one of the best ever,

00:05:44.176 --> 00:05:46.745
and your team
also did very well.

00:05:46.745 --> 00:05:48.180
It was a great job.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:53.752
I'd like to congratulate you
on a really great World Cup.

00:05:53.752 --> 00:05:56.054
One of the best ever,
from what everybody tells me.

00:05:56.054 --> 00:05:57.256
One of the best ever.

00:05:57.256 --> 00:06:00.092
And also for your team itself
doing so well.

00:06:00.092 --> 00:06:02.328
I watched quite a bit
in the United States.

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:03.495
We call it soccer.

00:06:03.495 --> 00:06:05.698
[ Laughter ]
-Everyone --

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:10.936
Everyone knows we call it soccer
in the United States.

00:06:10.936 --> 00:06:14.407
Trump's like a college sophomore
on his first trip abroad.

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:17.109
"You know, in America,
we call the loo a toilet."

00:06:17.109 --> 00:06:24.383
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.383 --> 00:06:26.185
But that doesn't
even begin to capture

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:27.520
how surreal this summit was.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.421
However low
your expectations were,

00:06:29.421 --> 00:06:30.822
Trump managed to go much lower.

00:06:30.822 --> 00:06:33.659
Because just three days
after the Justice Department

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:36.862
issued an indictment of 12
Russian intelligence officials,

00:06:36.862 --> 00:06:39.665
offering some of the most
specific evidence yet

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:42.000
of Russian meddling
in the 2016 election,

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.503
the President
of the United States

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:46.939
twisted himself in knots
to take Putin's side.

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:53.345
-Our relationship has never
been worse than it is now.

00:06:53.345 --> 00:06:59.118
However, that changed
as of about four hours ago.

00:06:59.118 --> 00:07:00.986
Our militaries
do get along very well.

00:07:00.986 --> 00:07:03.722
I think that the United States
has been foolish.

00:07:03.722 --> 00:07:05.624
I think we've all been foolish.

00:07:05.624 --> 00:07:07.760
There was no collusion at all.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:12.598
It came out as a reason why
the Democrats lost an election.

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:13.866
There was no collusion.

00:07:13.866 --> 00:07:15.534
I didn't know the president.

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:18.170
What happened
to Hillary Clinton's e-mails?

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:22.074
33,000 e-mails gone, just gone.

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:24.544
I think in Russia,
they wouldn't be gone so easily.

00:07:24.544 --> 00:07:26.912
President Putin
was extremely strong

00:07:26.912 --> 00:07:29.649
and powerful
in his denial today.

00:07:29.649 --> 00:07:31.651
He just said, "It's not Russia."

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:34.820
I will say this -- I don't
see any reason why it would be.

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:38.224
I'm sure we'll be meeting again
in the future, often.

00:07:38.224 --> 00:07:40.459
-Can someone get Trump
a glass of water?

00:07:40.459 --> 00:07:42.194
'Cause he thirsty.

00:07:42.194 --> 00:07:44.096
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:46.265
It's only a matter of weeks --

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:47.900
It's only a matter of weeks

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:50.502
before he
"Single White Females" Putin.

00:07:50.502 --> 00:07:53.105
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:56.708
"Do you like my haircut, Vlad?"

00:07:56.708 --> 00:07:58.844
So, just to recap,
Trump blamed the U.S.

00:07:58.844 --> 00:08:00.112
for Russian aggressions,

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:02.248
attacked the FBI and the
Special Counsel's investigation,

00:08:02.248 --> 00:08:04.283
took Putin's side
on election meddling,

00:08:04.283 --> 00:08:05.851
attacked Democrats
and Hillary Clinton

00:08:05.851 --> 00:08:07.085
with Putin standing next to him,

00:08:07.085 --> 00:08:08.820
and said Putin
was strong and powerful.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:12.458
Can you imagine what
their private meeting was like?

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:15.994
I'm worried he let Putin
annex one of the 50 states.

00:08:15.994 --> 00:08:18.564
"Here's an electoral map.
Pick one of the blue ones."

00:08:18.564 --> 00:08:19.665
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:21.267
Seriously,
Trump gushes over Putin

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:23.736
like a flustered 12-year-old who
just met Mickey at Disneyland.

00:08:23.736 --> 00:08:24.870
[ Laughter ]

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.505
and Putin treats him
like a 12-year-old,

00:08:26.505 --> 00:08:29.007
as evidenced by the gift
he gave the President.

00:08:29.007 --> 00:08:31.577
-President Trump
has just mentioned

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:36.182
that we've successfully
concluded the World Futbol Cup.

00:08:36.182 --> 00:08:40.319
Speaking of the futbol,
actually...

00:08:40.319 --> 00:08:42.555
Mr. President,
I'll give this ball to you,

00:08:42.555 --> 00:08:44.623
and now the ball
is in your court.

00:08:44.623 --> 00:08:49.795
[ Laughter ]

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:51.696
-That's right --
Putin got a propaganda victory,

00:08:51.696 --> 00:08:52.931
and we got a soccer ball.

00:08:52.931 --> 00:08:54.699
Do you really think Trump's
gonna play soccer?

00:08:54.699 --> 00:08:56.968
Look at him. The only way Trump
would ever get near

00:08:56.968 --> 00:08:59.405
a soccer pitch is if he could
stay in his golf cart.

00:08:59.405 --> 00:09:01.573
[ Laughter ]

00:09:01.573 --> 00:09:04.042
And it got worse from there,
because Trump went on

00:09:04.042 --> 00:09:06.278
to peddle an insane
conspiracy theory

00:09:06.278 --> 00:09:09.715
by implying something fishy
was going on with the DNC server

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:11.383
that was hacked by the Russians.

00:09:11.383 --> 00:09:12.851
-You have groups
that are wondering

00:09:12.851 --> 00:09:15.454
why the FBI
never took the server.

00:09:15.454 --> 00:09:17.189
Why haven't
they taken the server?

00:09:17.189 --> 00:09:18.791
Where is the server?

00:09:18.791 --> 00:09:20.826
I want to know,
where is the server,

00:09:20.826 --> 00:09:23.662
and what is the server saying?

00:09:23.662 --> 00:09:26.332
But I really do
want to see the server.

00:09:26.332 --> 00:09:29.735
I really believe that this will
probably go on for a while,

00:09:29.735 --> 00:09:32.371
but I don't think it can go on
without finding out

00:09:32.371 --> 00:09:34.439
what happened to the server.

00:09:34.439 --> 00:09:36.341
-Oh, my God.
He sounds like your uncle

00:09:36.341 --> 00:09:38.377
trying to get the waiter's
attention at a restaurant.

00:09:38.377 --> 00:09:39.511
[ Laughter ]

00:09:39.511 --> 00:09:42.448
"Where is the server?
I want more bread,

00:09:42.448 --> 00:09:45.117
and I don't have any ketchup
for my crumpets!"

00:09:45.117 --> 00:09:47.352
[ Laughter ]

00:09:47.352 --> 00:09:49.021
Of course, Trump's behavior
would be bizarre

00:09:49.021 --> 00:09:50.956
and suspicious on its own,
but we also know,

00:09:50.956 --> 00:09:52.358
thanks to Mueller's indictment

00:09:52.358 --> 00:09:54.560
of 12 Russian intelligence
operatives on Friday,

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:56.395
the Russian hackers
were not only helping Trump

00:09:56.395 --> 00:09:58.964
during the election
but responding directly to him

00:09:58.964 --> 00:10:00.399
when he issued
that infamous plea

00:10:00.399 --> 00:10:03.035
in the summer of 2016 to hack
Hillary Clinton's e-mails.

00:10:03.035 --> 00:10:04.403
You know, this one.

00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:06.339
-Russia, if you're listening,

00:10:06.339 --> 00:10:12.645
I hope you're able to find the
30,000 e-mails that are missing.

00:10:12.645 --> 00:10:13.946
-Remember when everyone was like

00:10:13.946 --> 00:10:16.882
"Ha ha! Russia's not
actually listening, right?"

00:10:16.882 --> 00:10:19.385
-It now appears
that Russia was listening.

00:10:19.385 --> 00:10:21.453
Because on that very same day,

00:10:21.453 --> 00:10:23.489
Russian officials
named in the indictment

00:10:23.489 --> 00:10:26.124
began hacking into
Clinton's server.

00:10:26.124 --> 00:10:28.961
-Not only were they listening,
they were taking orders.

00:10:28.961 --> 00:10:30.529
Everyone acted
like it was a joke,

00:10:30.529 --> 00:10:33.532
but Trump acted like
he was at a drive-through.

00:10:33.532 --> 00:10:36.235
"Uh, yeah, can I get
30,000 missing e-mails,

00:10:36.235 --> 00:10:39.105
illegal dirt on my opponent,
and as many Big Macs

00:10:39.105 --> 00:10:41.040
as you can fit
in this giant white hat?"

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.542
[ Laughter ]

00:10:43.542 --> 00:10:46.512
Now, even if we put aside
the mountains of evidence

00:10:46.512 --> 00:10:49.081
pointing toward collusion
or Trump's financial ties

00:10:49.081 --> 00:10:51.550
to Russian oligarchs
or the possibility that Russia

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:53.385
has compromising
information on him,

00:10:53.385 --> 00:10:55.554
there's also the fact
that Trump has a very clear

00:10:55.554 --> 00:10:58.190
personal affinity
for authoritarians like Putin.

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:00.058
Yesterday,
his National Security Advisor,

00:11:00.058 --> 00:11:01.760
John Bolton,
was asked specifically

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:03.462
about Trump's attacks
on the media

00:11:03.462 --> 00:11:06.165
and deflected
by talking about World War II.

00:11:06.165 --> 00:11:08.867
-Doesn't that contribute to
exactly the kind of undermining

00:11:08.867 --> 00:11:12.103
of the free press
that we see out of Russia?

00:11:12.103 --> 00:11:14.139
-No, I don't think that
has anything to do with it.

00:11:14.139 --> 00:11:16.642
And let's just be clear --
Franklin Roosevelt

00:11:16.642 --> 00:11:19.078
met with Joseph Stalin at a time

00:11:19.078 --> 00:11:23.415
when activity in Russia was
a lot worse than it is today.

00:11:23.415 --> 00:11:27.620
So, let's try and have some
historical perspective here

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:30.989
and not act like we have the
attention span of fruit flies.

00:11:30.989 --> 00:11:33.692
-We have the attention span
of fruit flies?

00:11:33.692 --> 00:11:37.796
The dude you work for thinks
Ireland is part of the U.K.

00:11:37.796 --> 00:11:39.598
And even a fruit fly
can remember

00:11:39.598 --> 00:11:41.433
to let the Queen go first.

00:11:41.433 --> 00:11:42.801
[ Laughter ]

00:11:42.801 --> 00:11:44.703
And on top of everything else,
today a Russian woman

00:11:44.703 --> 00:11:46.138
who tried to broker
a pair of secret meetings

00:11:46.138 --> 00:11:47.372
between Trump and Putin

00:11:47.372 --> 00:11:49.308
was charged and accused
of working with Americans

00:11:49.308 --> 00:11:50.942
to carry out
a secret Russian effort

00:11:50.942 --> 00:11:52.411
to influence American politics.

00:11:52.411 --> 00:11:54.012
So while that was happening,
Trump was doing

00:11:54.012 --> 00:11:56.648
everything he could to
ingratiate himself with Putin.

00:11:56.648 --> 00:11:58.016
He's selling out our democracy,

00:11:58.016 --> 00:11:59.451
and there's only
one word for it.

00:11:59.451 --> 00:12:00.685
-Heartbreaking.

00:12:00.685 --> 00:12:02.521
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:02.521 --> 00:12:05.891
[ Cheers and applause ]

